A||||2||Richard Parnell||poem||||1||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||01-05-2001||02:35 PM||||My walk on the mountain brought me to a new land<BR>This was a land of new vistas that I had heard rumors of<BR>Whispers of as a child<BR>But as a child and then a young man<BR>When I would approach to hear clearly what was said<BR>There would be a hush as if it were a secret that could not be shared<BR>This secret I thought must be one that loses it's power<BR>When overheard without invitation<BR>I became determined to discover this secret<BR>And would wander listening for the whispering<BR>Sometimes I would hear the suspiration<BR>And I knew it was a preparation<BR>To once again allow the mysterious to be known<BR>And would pause in my step so as to not miss the private thoughts<BR>Of the unknown that stands around each corner<BR>That would issue with the expiration of breath<BR>There were times that I thought I understood a snatch of words<BR>They were only bits and pieces of knowledge<BR>Never enough to lead me to understanding what the secret was<BR>As I grew I heard these whispers in many parts of the world<BR>At times you could just hear them in the forests<BR>Barely discernable from the wind<BR>Then again the whispers were as loud as roars to be heard<BR>Against the confounding chaos of war<BR>I would generally roam listening for the whispering alone<BR>Others would tire of the seeking<BR>Some would not believe that there were the secrets<BR>Some I believe may even have known what the secrets were<BR>But would not let me know<BR>Seeking to exclude one who could not clearly hear<BR>Obviously not worthy of the sharing of such a treasure<BR>The wandering brought me to many parts of life<BR>I met love<BR>I found friendship<BR>I discovered heartbreak and ecstasy<BR>But always I knew it was not complete without the words<BR>That I could never hear<BR>My life became full with the accoutrements of manhood<BR>I entered the world of the dealings of man<BR>And I no longer listened for the whispers<BR>The secret was forgotten even as it had never been learned<BR>Many years passed<BR>My life entered the middle grounds<BR>And many of the trappings that had occupied me for so many years<BR>Fell away as they wore to frays of what they once were<BR>I found myself naked to the glare of responsibilities of character<BR>And realized that I was lacking<BR>I had forgotten about what was important<BR>I never had completed the journey that I had set upon<BR>So many years ago<BR>If I had kept a part of that wonder with me I thought<BR>Things would have been different<BR>But there is no truth in that<BR>You can not know when you have lost something<BR>That you were never aware of possessing<BR>So I began another journey<BR>A journey not so great in miles<BR>But greater in distance than all the wanderings of my youth<BR>This journey brought me to the edge of the light of what<BR>I thought was enlightenment<BR>I was wrong but I was aware<BR>I began to try and chase down an echo<BR>Not knowing that it would lead to frustration and madness<BR>I would hear myself speak and try to catch the words to make them correct<BR>Chasing the sound of my ignorance through the ears of another<BR>Brought me to display myself through acts that<BR>Contradicted all I tried to say<BR>The eyes that were upon me could not understand the tongues I spoke<BR>Nor the dance I performed<BR>I was the grace of all dance and the brute of gracelessness<BR>I would enter each movement without regard<BR>To the sensibilities of other dwellers of this land<BR>I became a leper of the heart<BR>Shunned by the very emotions I was consuming<BR>Wise women and foolish men helped to guide me<BR>Leading me through many doors at once<BR>I found myself looking at pieces of myself<BR>Spread across distances that I could barely conceive<BR>Yet my arms could reach to each of my myriad of selves with ease<BR>Encompassing each with a despairing reassurance of confusion<BR>How could I ever know myself again<BR>I had deceived myself for so long that I no longer recognized myself<BR>How can you heal a stranger<BR>One that you do not even know where his pain is<BR>Someone whose language you do not understand<BR>Let alone speak<BR>Dishonesty brought me to this state<BR>Not the companion that I had known all my life<BR>Not the dishonesty of protection<BR>The one that was my ally in my youth<BR>The one that shielded me from prying eyes<BR>This new one was a distant relative of that friend<BR>This one lied to me<BR>This one betrayed me and let me lie to myself<BR>Thinking I was still the person I was so long ago<BR>Thinking I still had the world fooled<BR>Under my control<BR>The fool in truth was staring me in the face<BR>Each time I looked in the mirror now<BR>And I was so sure of myself<BR>Using the tendrils of perception that still remained from long ago<BR>To convince myself that I still possessed the power of my youth and ignorance<BR>The power to make my world as I wanted<BR>That world grasped me by the scruff as I passed in a flailing frenzy<BR>And threw me to the ground<BR>I realized the world that I thought mine<BR>Was as a glass ball self enclosed<BR>A capsule with no bearing on the universe<BR>Other than the ability to receive a shake from life from time to time<BR>The time between shakes was long<BR>The snow had never been disturbed<BR>My crash to earth shattered my reality<BR>My perceptions had been so narrow as to have no notions<BR>Not a hint that others also danced<BR>With my universe pierced the whispering became clear<BR>The words were deafening and confounding<BR>The unknown around the corner was now standing before me<BR>Screaming the whispers I so wanted to hear in my youth<BR>The dreams of youth had become a reality of nightmares<BR>My nakedness would not let me accept the truth<BR>The words I had once craved were ignored in my attempt to cover my shame<BR>My shame deflected me<BR>Again I could not hear the words<BR>I was deaf in my blindness<BR>The calmness of solitude was a shrieking cacophony of confusion<BR>The turmoil of the masses became a quiet refuge<BR>I stumbled out the doorway and found myself able to hear<BR>Wandering through the corridors of unfamiliar humanity<BR>I was handed the elixir that I had been so fond of for ages<BR>It tasted vile and was unpleasant in it's effect<BR>I found confusion and madness were residents of this world also<BR>But here I could make choices<BR>I grasped at the promise that clarity offered and found it refreshing<BR>I found I had been burning the houses of my fellows to preserve mine<BR>I was shamed by the words I began to hear from the whispers<BR>They were words that I had heard before but chose to ignore<BR>As not fitting my perception of the world<BR>The fear of truth and responsibility that youth feels<BR>Had never been overcome<BR>I was still a babe<BR>My image in the looking glass had been painted on<BR>And was now flaking off from the force of the glare of close inspection<BR>What I see is not frightening<BR>It is not what I expected but knowing nothing I had expected nothing<BR>I had been proud that I was the same<BR>I had been proud that I had not changed<BR>My pride had hardened me<BR>Made me blind and deaf<BR>The bareness that I now display to the world is all I deserve<BR>It is a gift<BR>It is enough<BR>Yeah right, I’m so full of crap<BR>||||reg||1
